# Parse-analyzer — dev context

## Stack
- **Next.js 14** (Pages Router). App code lives under `src/`. [`src/pages/index.tsx`](src/pages/index.tsx) is **Analyze** at `/` with **Solo** | **Compare** subtabs (player-1-only vs side-by-side); [`src/pages/analyze.tsx`](src/pages/analyze.tsx) redirects to `/`. [`src/components/analyze/SoloFightView/`](src/components/analyze/SoloFightView/) and [`CompareFightView/`](src/components/analyze/CompareFightView/) hold the two bodies. [`src/pages/_app.tsx`](src/pages/_app.tsx) wraps `AppSessionProvider` → `AnalyzePageCacheProvider` → **`FightAnalysisProvider`** (WCL URL, load, dual chat threads, `analysisSubtab`, auth). [`src/components/AppNav/`](src/components/AppNav/) is route tabs + the **Settings** dropdown (WCL status row, Claude key, theme radios); the WCL URL bar is [`src/components/analyze/WclLoadPanel/`](src/components/analyze/WclLoadPanel/) on Analyze only. [`src/pages/reports.tsx`](src/pages/reports.tsx) is the **Reports** browser (my/guild logs → pulls → player picker → `loadCompare(url)`; queries in [`src/lib/wclReports.ts`](src/lib/wclReports.ts), incl. `characterRankings` "top parse" compare). **WCL auth is per-user and required**: everyone must **Sign in with WarcraftLogs** ([`src/lib/wclUserToken.ts`](src/lib/wclUserToken.ts), PKCE via `/api/auth`); the token lives in that browser's localStorage only, is sent as `x-wcl-user-token`, and `/api/wcl` requires it (401 otherwise), targeting WCL's `/api/v2/user` endpoint (user's permissions + rate limit); `ensureFreshWclUser()` silently renews it via the stored OAuth refresh token (`/api/auth` `user-refresh`) on `useWclUser` mount and before every `gql()`. [`src/lib/serverWclToken.ts`](src/lib/serverWclToken.ts) `getWclToken()` (client-credentials from `WCL_CLIENT_ID`/`WCL_CLIENT_SECRET`) is only for game-data routes (`/api/talents`, `/api/debug-tree`). Shared UI primitives (PageHeader/Panel/FieldRow/KeyField/OrDivider/Accordion) live in [`src/components/ui/`](src/components/ui/) — use them for new page chrome. Shared atoms are [`src/styles/ui.module.css`](src/styles/ui.module.css). Themes: 3 vibes in [`src/lib/vibes.ts`](src/lib/vibes.ts) (`slate` default via `:root`, `classic`, `light` as `html[data-vibe=…]` overrides).
- **Claude**: [`src/lib/wclClient/index.ts`](src/lib/wclClient/index.ts) `callAI()` / `callAIStream()` POST to [`src/pages/api/ai.ts`](src/pages/api/ai.ts); the model id is the **single constant** in [`src/lib/wclClient/anthropicModel.ts`](src/lib/wclClient/anthropicModel.ts) — never hardcode model strings elsewhere. Fight text is built by [`src/lib/buildContext/index.ts`](src/lib/buildContext/index.ts) `buildRichContext()` (compare) or `buildRichContextPlayerOne()` (analyze tab) and sent as the **system** prompt. Ask Claude sections are gated on the browser-stored BYOK key via [`src/lib/claudeKeyBus.ts`](src/lib/claudeKeyBus.ts) (`useClaudeKeyPresent`, open-settings/key-changed window events); uncaught render errors hit [`src/components/AppErrorBoundary/`](src/components/AppErrorBoundary/).

## Critical: client-side context
- `buildRichContext` / `buildRichContextPlayerOne` run in the **browser** (from `FightAnalysisContext`). **Do not** use `fs` or server-only reads for prompt text. Static knowledge must be **imported** from bundled modules (e.g. [`src/lib/knowledge/embeddedGuides.ts`](src/lib/knowledge/embeddedGuides.ts), [`src/lib/knowledge/embeddedSimc.ts`](src/lib/knowledge/embeddedSimc.ts), [`src/lib/knowledge/embeddedWowhead.ts`](src/lib/knowledge/embeddedWowhead.ts) — JSON snapshots under [`knowledge/wowhead/scraped/`](knowledge/wowhead/scraped/)).

## Knowledge corpora
- **Wowhead summaries**: [`knowledge/guides/`](knowledge/guides/) — **Wowhead-only** authoring policy; see [`knowledge/guides/README.md`](knowledge/guides/README.md). Sync human markdown → [`src/lib/knowledge/embeddedGuides.ts`](src/lib/knowledge/embeddedGuides.ts) when editing bodies.
- **SimulationCraft APL**: vendored `.simc` under [`knowledge/simc/`](knowledge/simc/) — **all 34 specs with an upstream default APL** (no healers). After changing files, run **`npm run embed-simc`** to regenerate the **generated** [`src/lib/knowledge/embeddedSimcData.ts`](src/lib/knowledge/embeddedSimcData.ts) (never hand-edit; the spec table lives in `scripts/embed-simc.mjs`, prompt logic in [`embeddedSimc.ts`](src/lib/knowledge/embeddedSimc.ts)). GPL-3.0 upstream; see [`knowledge/simc/README.md`](knowledge/simc/README.md). The SimC block is **opt-in** in the UI (`simcCompareEnabled`) unless the user sends the **SimC + Wowhead** preset, which forces SimC when available for the spec.
- **Wowhead scraped guides**: JSON under [`knowledge/wowhead/scraped/`](knowledge/wowhead/scraped/) via **`npm run scrape-wowhead -- <spec-folder…|--all>`** (table-driven registry in `scripts/wowhead/scrape-wowhead.mjs`). Bundled for Claude in [`src/lib/knowledge/embeddedWowhead.ts`](src/lib/knowledge/embeddedWowhead.ts) (`SPEC_DOCS` registry). Opt-in via preset `PRESET_CASTS_VS_SIMC_WOWHEAD` in [`src/lib/prompts/chatPresets.ts`](src/lib/prompts/chatPresets.ts) (forces SimC + Wowhead context for that message). Covers **all 40 retail specs** incl. Midnight's Devourer DH (registries in the scraper and `embeddedWowhead.ts` `SPEC_DOCS`; coverage locked by `src/lib/knowledge/__tests__/embeddedWowhead.test.ts`).
- Class reference (Wowhead summary) uses **`talentDiff.specId`** when present. SimC embed matches specs listed in [`embeddedSimc.ts`](src/lib/knowledge/embeddedSimc.ts).

## Fight pipeline (for context changes)
- WCL fetch/process: [`src/lib/fightAnalysis/`](src/lib/fightAnalysis/), game state: [`src/lib/gameState/`](src/lib/gameState/). Rich prompt sections use [`src/lib/buildContext/formatters.ts`](src/lib/buildContext/formatters.ts).

## SimulationCraft upstream (simulationcraft/simc, branch `midnight`)
Facts from the SimC repo READMEs—use so we don’t misuse vendored APL files:

- **`ActionPriorityLists/`** holds **generated** raw APL text (`.simc`). Upstream says these files **must not be manually edited**; they are produced from **`engine/class_modules/`** and **`engine/class_modules/apl/`** (C++ / converter pipeline).
- **`ActionPriorityLists/default/`** — default lists per spec/module from that generation path.
- **`ActionPriorityLists/assisted_combat/`** — lists derived from Blizzard **DBC** tables (`AssistedCombat`, `AssistedCombatStep`, `AssistedCombatRule`), not the same as `default/`.
- **APL snippet shape** (for reading/parsing): lines like `actions=…`, `actions+=/spell,if=condition`, named lists `actions.list+=/…`, comments `# …`. Not a full SimC **profile** (gear/talents/options)—those are separate.
- **This app**: we **vendor snapshots** (e.g. `knowledge/simc/mage_frost.midnight.simc`) for Claude context. Refresh by re-downloading **raw** `midnight` URLs and `npm run embed-simc`—do not treat our copy as the place to “fix” SimC’s canonical APL (real fixes belong upstream in SimC).
- **Docs / community**: SimC wiki (starters guide, common issues), Discord **SimCMinMax** — for semantics disputes, not for embedding whole dumps into parse-ai.

## Conventions
- **Code style lives in [CODE_STYLE.md](CODE_STYLE.md)** (+ condensed `.cursor/rules/code-style.mdc`): new files follow it fully; existing files keep their local style until substantially reworked.
- Prefer **small, focused diffs**; match existing patterns in touched files.
- Run **`npm run build`** (and tests if touching logic) before finishing.
- **Session checkpoint**: [`PROGRESS.md`](PROGRESS.md) records where the last session left off and what still needs testing — read it when resuming work, and update it when the state changes.
